    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "The naive L2 error at $t=10$ on the finest grid will be $\\sim10^{-3}$–$10^{-4}$ (dominated by accumulated phase drift of the soliton position/phase), failing the $10^{-6}$ target; the phase-aligned (symmetry-adapted) L2 error will be $\\sim10^{-7}$–$10^{-9}$, meeting the $10^{-8}$ target; mass/energy/momentum drifts will be $\\le10^{-10}$ (spectral) and $\\le10^{-7}$ (CN), confirming they are independent error indicators; the naive/aligned ratio will exceed $10^2$, demonstrating the symmetry-adapted metric is **not** a renaming of the naive tolerance. Convergence order will be $\\ge2$ in space and time for both integrators, and the Richardson estimate will agree with the phase-aligned error to within a factor of 3."
